course: dictionary
lesson: 4326
title: Growth in context
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Growth is a noun, and it has more than one meaning. Context tells you which one. Read the words around it: «Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth» is about a tree getting bigger over the years, not about a lump.
explain: «In deep sleep the body releases most of its growth hormone.» Here growth means getting bigger and more developed, the way a body grows. Ask yourself what the sentence says growth is doing, then swap your meaning in and check it still makes sense.
explain: Growth can also mean an increase in amount, as in «population growth», or a lump that grows on the skin. Science, maths and health use the word in different ways, so always look at the clues around it.
fact: Growth means getting bigger, taller or more developed.
fact: «Growth» can also mean an increase in amount, such as population growth.
fact: A growth spurt is a quick time when a child gets taller fast.
fact: «A growth» can also mean a lump, or something that grows on the skin.
fact: Children aged 9 to 12 need about 9 to 12 hours of sleep a night.
exercise: «Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth.» What does growth mean here? | A broken branch | *Getting bigger over time | A lump on the tree | A sunny day
exercise: «Plants need light and water for growth.» What does growth mean in this sentence? | Sleeping in the dark | *Getting bigger and developing | A lump on a plant | A type of soil
exercise: Sam says growth only means a lump. Is he right? | No, growth means a long sleep | *No, growth can also mean getting bigger or an increase in amount | Only in science lessons | Yes, growth always means a lump
test: «Population growth» in a text means what? | A broken bone | A weak plant | *An increase in the number of people | A lump on the skin
test: Which phrase means a quick time when a child gets taller fast? | *A growth spurt | A dry year | Population growth | A growth plate
exam: Which meaning of growth fits «Each ring in a tree stump is one year of growth» best? | An increase in people | A break from sleep | A lump on a tree | *Getting bigger over time
